===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|pre|historic|t1=[[before]]}}, ''q.v.'', similar to slightly earlier {{m|en|ante-historic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ɒrɪk}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|properly}} Of or relating to the [[epoch]] before written [[record]].
#* '''1832''' October, ''Foreign Quarterly Review'', p. 369:
#*: Was it then in a '''pre-historic''' time that the Romans wandered into these lands?
# {{lb|en|inexact|_|or|_|jocular}} {{syn of|en|ancient|nodot=a}}: [[very]] [[old]], [[nonmodern]], [[unfashionable]], etc.

